 "statement": "MODEL STUDY on one short recording (minutes, see each run): far too short for any conclusion about profitability, one time of day, one volatility regime. No trade and no queue position was observed: a fill is a rule applied to two consecutive snapshots. `cross` under-counts fills (a quote can trade without the opposite best price reaching it between two snapshots) and `touch` over-counts them (it assumes the front of the queue). Fills at the snapshot cadence ignore everything that happens between snapshots. Maker fees are the venue table's base tier; no rebate. Nothing here can be executed by the wallet today: the agent path has no resting orders."
